# Web client

- The only UI: React 19, TypeScript (strict), Vite, Tailwind v4, Radix dialogs, TanStack Query, TanStack Router (code-based route tree in `src/router.tsx`, routes code-split with `lazyRouteComponent`), TanStack Virtual for log windowing.
- Wiring: `src/main.tsx` builds `AppServices` (`src/app/services.ts`: API client, endpoints, `SessionStore`, `SessionRefresher`, QueryClient) and renders `AppRoot`, which reacts to session events. Tests build the same services over a fake `Transport`; never add module-level singletons.
- API layer (`src/api`): `client.ts` is the only code that calls `fetch`/`XMLHttpRequest`; every failure is an `ApiError` (`errors.ts`) parsed from the error envelope or mapped to `network_error`/`invalid_response`/`aborted`. Components show `describeError(err)` and the request id, never response text. All wire types come from `types.gen.ts` (generated; run `scripts/gen-types.sh`). Add routes to `endpoints.ts`, query keys to `query-keys.ts`, hooks to `queries.ts`.
- Session: token in memory, mirrored to sessionStorage (default) or localStorage ("Keep me signed in"), key `golem_deploy_session`; tabs sync over the `golem_deploy_session` BroadcastChannel. A 401 `unauthenticated` for the current token ends the session once (`SessionStore.handleUnauthenticated`). `SessionRefresher` refreshes 30 minutes before the JWT `exp` and on tab return after long inactivity. The displayed role comes from `GET /account`, never from the JWT.
- Credentials only as `Authorization: Bearer`; never cookies. Streams (job logs, server logs) use `client.stream` + `readLines` (`src/api/stream.ts`) through `useLogStream`; the contract has no resume offset, so streams are not auto-reconnected.
- React Query: no retry on 4xx, polling only for state that changes on its own (active jobs, busy projects, server lists/state, stats, status) and only while visible. Per-row actions own their mutation so pending state stays per row. Every job-returning action shows the job inline (`InlineJob`).
- UI primitives live in `src/components/ui`; reuse them instead of new class strings. Render server strings as text; no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; links from server data go through `safeHttpUrl`.
- The daemon serves the SPA with a strict CSP (`script-src 'self'`, `connect-src 'self'`, no external origins). Keep the build free of inline scripts, eval and remote assets.
- Mock layer: `src/mock/transport.ts` simulates the not-yet-implemented routes under `VITE_API_MOCK=1 npm run dev` (`GOLEM_DEPLOY_DEV_API` overrides the dev proxy target). It is imported only behind `import.meta.env.DEV`; `vite.config.ts` refuses to build with the flag and fails if the mock reaches the bundle. Remove a domain from the mock once the daemon implements it.
- Verification: `npm run lint` (zero warnings), `npm test` (Vitest + Testing Library, jsdom), `npm run build` (type-check + bundle for Go embedding).
